1
00:00:03,223 --> 00:00:04,933
Damn, it's pouring.

2
00:00:05,934 --> 00:00:09,521
[shivers]
I'm cold. I'm so gonna get sick.

3
00:00:09,604 --> 00:00:11,523
Maybe I should just go home.

4
00:00:11,606 --> 00:00:13,442
But what about that awful thing?

5
00:00:15,569 --> 00:00:16,570
ROACHES ARE UNSEEMLY,
SO INSTEAD, CAKE! YOU'RE WELCOME!

6
00:00:16,653 --> 00:00:17,738
[moans]

7
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:20,407
[sneezes]

8
00:00:22,284 --> 00:00:23,118
Huh?

9
00:00:28,832 --> 00:00:29,666
Hmm.

10
00:00:31,585 --> 00:00:32,502
Uh…

11
00:00:33,295 --> 00:00:34,129
Oh, crap.

12
00:00:39,217 --> 00:00:40,302
-Hey.
-[shrieks]

13
00:00:41,344 --> 00:00:43,138
Are you a runaway?

14
00:00:43,221 --> 00:00:44,389
[scoffs]
No.

15
00:00:45,766 --> 00:00:48,060
[Tsukasa] No judgments,
you need to stay dry out here,

16
00:00:48,143 --> 00:00:51,688
but you do know there's been reports
of a creep in the park the last few days?

17
00:00:51,772 --> 00:00:53,690
What? No way!
[grunts]

18
00:00:54,232 --> 00:00:55,609
[groans]

19
00:00:56,860 --> 00:00:58,278
-Thanks for the head-ups.
-Huh?

20
00:00:58,361 --> 00:00:59,780
Uh, hey, wait.

21
00:01:00,447 --> 00:01:01,782
[grunts]

22
00:01:01,865 --> 00:01:03,450
Keep your hands off!

23
00:01:04,951 --> 00:01:06,078
-Huh?
-Here, take it.

24
00:01:06,578 --> 00:01:08,663
[bright music]

25
00:01:10,749 --> 00:01:14,920
[Riri] Borrow it, return it,
let the sparks fly.

26
00:01:16,088 --> 00:01:18,840
-Mm-mm. No thanks.
-[Tsukasa] Why?

27
00:01:19,341 --> 00:01:21,593
[Anzu] Because then, you'll get drenched.

28
00:01:21,676 --> 00:01:24,012
[Tsukasa] Don't worry.
I live really close.

29
00:01:24,095 --> 00:01:25,597
[grunts]
Seriously!

30
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,725
I already owe you for breaking your phone.

31
00:01:28,809 --> 00:01:31,061
I said it was okay. Just take it.

32
00:01:31,144 --> 00:01:33,855
You're going to
get sick out here like this.

33
00:01:35,273 --> 00:01:38,068
Well, I'm so slow,
I couldn't catch a cold.

34
00:01:38,151 --> 00:01:39,694
[Tsukasa] Your nose is running.

35
00:01:39,778 --> 00:01:43,698
-And you were sneezing earlier.
-It's none of your business, okay?

36
00:01:44,282 --> 00:01:46,159
Stop being so stubborn.

37
00:01:46,743 --> 00:01:48,703
-Ugh, fine! Come to my place.
-Huh! What?

38
00:01:49,287 --> 00:01:52,541
[Tsukasa] I've got an extra umbrella
I was going to toss. You can take that.

39
00:01:52,624 --> 00:01:54,209
[Anzu] Um, but…

40
00:01:56,044 --> 00:01:58,630
Listen, if you're worried about owing me…

41
00:01:58,713 --> 00:01:59,548
[Anzu] Hey…

42
00:02:00,048 --> 00:02:01,591
…then just come on already.

43
00:02:01,675 --> 00:02:04,219
-[Anzu] Oh, okay.
-[Tsukasa] Let's go.

44
00:02:04,302 --> 00:02:06,179
[gasps]

45
00:02:06,263 --> 00:02:07,722
[Anzu] Your hand…

46
00:02:09,307 --> 00:02:10,475
[exclaims]

47
00:02:13,603 --> 00:02:15,772
I'm sorry,
but you took forever to take it.

48
00:02:15,856 --> 00:02:18,650
[Anzu] Hey, wait up!
Now, you're getting wet.

49
00:02:18,733 --> 00:02:19,901
[grunts]

50
00:02:19,985 --> 00:02:22,904
[Anzu] Sorry, you're just really tall.

51
00:02:23,864 --> 00:02:24,906
[Anzu gasps]

52
00:02:27,033 --> 00:02:28,368
There! Problem solved.

53
00:02:29,035 --> 00:02:31,163
-Yeah.
-Come on then.

54
00:02:33,707 --> 00:02:35,083
[Anzu] This is every girl's dream.

55
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:38,044
A hot guy sharing his umbrella

56
00:02:38,128 --> 00:02:41,673
as you walk shoulder to shoulder
in the rain.

57
00:02:41,756 --> 00:02:44,634
Ugh, I will not give in!

58
00:02:44,718 --> 00:02:46,595
[evil laughter]

59
00:02:52,309 --> 00:02:54,311
[theme music]

60
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:19,479
#2 IT'S TIME FOR CHILDREN
TO GO TO SLEEP

61
00:04:19,562 --> 00:04:20,730
[Tsukasa] Wait there a sec.

62
00:04:22,774 --> 00:04:25,944
[Anzu] He's hot and he lives alone.

63
00:04:26,027 --> 00:04:26,987
[gulps]

64
00:04:28,488 --> 00:04:31,283
No. I will not fall for this obvious trap.

65
00:04:31,366 --> 00:04:34,369
Just think about
your favorite game characters.

66
00:04:34,869 --> 00:04:36,413
-[sighs happily]
-[Tsukasa] Here.

67
00:04:36,496 --> 00:04:38,164
-[Anzu groans]
-[Tsukasa] You should dry off

68
00:04:38,248 --> 00:04:39,291
before you go.

69
00:04:39,374 --> 00:04:41,042
[Anzu] I've got this.

70
00:04:41,126 --> 00:04:43,295
Hot guy blurring filter.

71
00:04:47,632 --> 00:04:49,801
Yeah, that's better.

72
00:04:50,385 --> 00:04:51,469
[Anzu] Thanks.

73
00:04:52,012 --> 00:04:55,181
Not my business, but why
were you hiding in the park anyway?

74
00:04:55,265 --> 00:05:00,145
[Anzu] Hm, actually, there's this thing
at my place, a ro… ro…

75
00:05:00,228 --> 00:05:02,814
-It's too terrifying. I can't even say it.
-Huh?

76
00:05:02,897 --> 00:05:03,940
Robber?

77
00:05:04,024 --> 00:05:06,568
Much worse, a roach!
[shrieks]

78
00:05:07,152 --> 00:05:08,320
I said it.

79
00:05:09,362 --> 00:05:11,323
You let a bug chase you out of your house?

80
00:05:12,365 --> 00:05:15,201
It's not just "a bug", it was gigantic!

81
00:05:15,285 --> 00:05:16,119
[groans]

82
00:05:16,202 --> 00:05:20,623
My mom usually handles
this sort of thing or my cat,

83
00:05:20,707 --> 00:05:24,127
but my parents moved
overseas for work with the cat.

84
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:27,213
First, the bug spray was empty,

85
00:05:27,297 --> 00:05:29,799
then, that thing came right for me,

86
00:05:29,883 --> 00:05:33,011
so I ran as fast as I could.
[whimpers]

87
00:05:33,094 --> 00:05:37,807
I forgot my wallet and my phone.
Then it started raining.

88
00:05:39,392 --> 00:05:43,271
Ugh, it's the worst night ever.
[whimpers]

89
00:05:45,065 --> 00:05:46,691
Your face…
[laughs]

90
00:05:46,775 --> 00:05:49,277
-[Anzu] Rude!
-[Tsukasa] I'm sorry.

91
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:53,114
[Anzu] I thought he was the quiet type
who doesn't smile much but…

92
00:05:53,865 --> 00:05:55,700
That sounds like a nightmare.

93
00:05:56,659 --> 00:05:58,912
-[glass shattering]
-[yells]

94
00:05:58,995 --> 00:06:00,705
No!

95
00:06:01,664 --> 00:06:03,708
He broke down my barrier.

96
00:06:03,792 --> 00:06:05,585
You leave me no choice.

97
00:06:06,127 --> 00:06:08,463
Come forth, Momohiki!

98
00:06:08,546 --> 00:06:10,256
[crackling]

99
00:06:12,092 --> 00:06:13,885
-[meows]
-[gasps]

100
00:06:14,844 --> 00:06:17,430
I guess that explains the mix-match shoes.

101
00:06:17,514 --> 00:06:20,016
[Anzu] It's working! Great job, Momohiki.

102
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:23,061
-[Tsukasa] Want me to get rid of it?
-Huh?

103
00:06:24,104 --> 00:06:25,814
Want me to get rid of it for you?

104
00:06:25,897 --> 00:06:28,441
You know,
the thing that shall not be mentioned.

105
00:06:28,525 --> 00:06:29,526
-For real?
-[gasps]

106
00:06:30,777 --> 00:06:32,529
[Anzu] No, I'm in too deep already.

107
00:06:34,197 --> 00:06:36,074
No, I got this.

108
00:06:37,117 --> 00:06:39,994
Are you trying to avoid me or something?

109
00:06:40,537 --> 00:06:43,039
[Anzu] What? Of course not!

110
00:06:43,623 --> 00:06:46,960
[Tsukasa] If this is about
breaking my phone, don't worry about it.

111
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:49,879
I was thinking about
getting a new one, anyway.

112
00:06:50,713 --> 00:06:51,548
Uh, um…

113
00:06:52,048 --> 00:06:55,385
I mean, seriously,
when you outright avoid me like that,

114
00:06:55,969 --> 00:06:57,387
it makes me feel anxious.

115
00:06:57,470 --> 00:06:59,764
[Anzu] "Make me feel anxious"?

116
00:07:00,348 --> 00:07:02,267
Well, if you don't want my help…

117
00:07:02,350 --> 00:07:06,729
No, really… I… need help.

118
00:07:07,313 --> 00:07:09,190
-[Tsukasa] All right, let's go.
-Huh…

119
00:07:10,150 --> 00:07:12,152
[cheerful music]

120
00:07:12,235 --> 00:07:14,154
Here, it's cold. Wear this.

121
00:07:14,237 --> 00:07:16,072
[Momohiki meows]

122
00:07:16,865 --> 00:07:20,535
How does he keep doing that?

123
00:07:20,618 --> 00:07:23,163
-[screaming in anger]
-[moans]

124
00:07:27,125 --> 00:07:29,043
[Tsukasa] So, where is it?

125
00:07:29,669 --> 00:07:31,546
I saw it in the kitchen before.

126
00:07:35,133 --> 00:07:38,052
[Anzu] There's a hot guy in my house.

127
00:07:39,053 --> 00:07:40,305
[Tsukasa] I don't see it.

128
00:07:41,639 --> 00:07:44,017
[Anzu] This is way too ridiculous.

129
00:07:44,642 --> 00:07:45,768
[exclaims]

130
00:07:47,061 --> 00:07:49,063
[suspenseful music]

131
00:07:49,981 --> 00:07:50,899
[shrieks]

132
00:07:53,193 --> 00:07:54,944
-[yells]
-[grunts]

133
00:07:56,154 --> 00:07:56,988
[thudding]

134
00:07:58,156 --> 00:08:01,534
It's right there! It's right there!

135
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:07,081
My bad, just a lens cap.
Who the heck left that thing here?

136
00:08:07,665 --> 00:08:08,666
[groans]

137
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:11,503
-Did you just freak out over…
-[both gasp]

138
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:15,423
[Anzu breathes shakily]
How…

139
00:08:18,259 --> 00:08:20,845
How did we end up like this?

140
00:08:20,929 --> 00:08:24,098
[narrator] Roaches are unseemly,
so instead, cake. You're welcome.

141
00:08:24,974 --> 00:08:26,351
-[shrieks]
-[grunts]

142
00:08:28,186 --> 00:08:31,105
-Go get it! Go get it!
-[Tsukasa grunts, gasps]

143
00:08:31,189 --> 00:08:32,607
[Tsukasa] That bastard!

144
00:08:34,025 --> 00:08:34,859
[Tsukasa grunts]

145
00:08:36,653 --> 00:08:38,071
[grunting continues]

146
00:08:38,571 --> 00:08:39,572
[whimpers]

147
00:08:40,281 --> 00:08:41,366
Piece of cake!

148
00:08:41,449 --> 00:08:43,993
[squeals]
Throw it away! Throw it away!

149
00:08:44,077 --> 00:08:45,995
[rain splatters]

150
00:08:46,079 --> 00:08:49,249
[Anzu] Thanks for helping
and sorry about stepping on you.

151
00:08:49,332 --> 00:08:51,501
[Tsukasa] Seriously, don't mention it.

152
00:08:51,584 --> 00:08:53,878
See you at school, Hoshino.

153
00:08:53,962 --> 00:08:56,506
Wait? How do you know my name?

154
00:08:57,257 --> 00:08:59,008
-Nameplate.
-Oh…

155
00:08:59,968 --> 00:09:02,011
Right.
[chuckles awkwardly]

156
00:09:02,095 --> 00:09:05,348
Tsukasa Kazuki. We go to the same school.

157
00:09:06,099 --> 00:09:08,935
-[Anzu] Right. I'm Class 2.
-I'm Class 7.

158
00:09:09,519 --> 00:09:12,021
Do me a favor, don't avoid me anymore.

159
00:09:12,105 --> 00:09:14,190
[gasps, sucks teeth]
Right.

160
00:09:14,774 --> 00:09:18,152
-Oh, can I at least wash your--
-No. Really. It's fine.

161
00:09:20,530 --> 00:09:24,033
Anyway, it might be a good idea
to take a nice warm bath.

162
00:09:24,117 --> 00:09:26,035
And be sure to bundle up.

163
00:09:26,119 --> 00:09:27,245
Yes, dad.

164
00:09:28,246 --> 00:09:30,456
And you be sure
to eat something hot tonight.

165
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,041
All right, Kazuki?

166
00:09:32,125 --> 00:09:33,876
[Tsukasa] Okay, mom.
[chuckles]

167
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:34,836
Later.

168
00:09:35,545 --> 00:09:37,046
-[wind whooshing]
-[both gasp]

169
00:09:37,130 --> 00:09:38,673
[effort grunts]

170
00:09:39,173 --> 00:09:40,425
[Tsukasa exhales deeply]

171
00:09:40,508 --> 00:09:42,176
[breathes nervously]

172
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:45,930
-Guess I could run for it.
-Uh, well, this sucks.

173
00:09:46,014 --> 00:09:48,433
[Tsukasa] I'll be fine. See ya.

174
00:09:48,516 --> 00:09:50,018
-[wind whooshing]
-[grunts]

175
00:09:50,101 --> 00:09:51,436
-[glass shatters]
-[both yelp]

176
00:09:57,025 --> 00:09:59,819
Officials are expecting
the storm to last all night.

177
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:04,824
A city-wide warning is in effect.
People have been asked to remain indoors,

178
00:10:04,907 --> 00:10:08,453
and avoid driving
in these severely dangerous conditions.

179
00:10:09,037 --> 00:10:11,039
[sighs]
Well, that's just great.

180
00:10:13,207 --> 00:10:15,209
A DREAM HOME

181
00:10:15,293 --> 00:10:18,921
[Anzu] This is my mom
and dad's dream house, their forever home.

182
00:10:19,005 --> 00:10:22,216
And they totally entrusted me
to take care of it while they're gone.

183
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:26,054
Now, look at it!
Not only does this freaky weather

184
00:10:26,137 --> 00:10:28,389
crashed the tree
right into the front door,

185
00:10:28,473 --> 00:10:30,850
it also has me
stranded inside until it blows over.

186
00:10:31,392 --> 00:10:35,855
Stuck here with a super cute guy
standing right there in the living room.

187
00:10:36,773 --> 00:10:40,652
Wait a sec… Is this becoming…

188
00:10:40,735 --> 00:10:43,655
a sleepover situation?

189
00:10:43,738 --> 00:10:44,739
[both giggling]

190
00:10:44,822 --> 00:10:47,325
No way he can spend the night.

191
00:10:47,408 --> 00:10:49,243
We barely even know each other.

192
00:10:49,327 --> 00:10:51,204
-Let's go, Anzu!
-[groaning]

193
00:10:51,287 --> 00:10:53,331
-[Anzu] I am so not ready for this…
-Let's go, Anzu! Go!

194
00:10:53,414 --> 00:10:55,500
[Anzu]
This was that thing's plan all along.

195
00:10:55,583 --> 00:10:57,502
[stomach rumbles]

196
00:10:57,585 --> 00:10:58,544
[gasps]

197
00:10:59,629 --> 00:11:01,089
Yeah, I'm hungry too.

198
00:11:01,714 --> 00:11:05,009
-I guess I'd better make some dinner.
-You're sure?

199
00:11:05,093 --> 00:11:07,553
[Anzu] Consider it a thank you
for getting rid of that bug.

200
00:11:09,597 --> 00:11:13,017
Problem is… what do I make?

201
00:11:13,643 --> 00:11:14,852
Let me see here.

202
00:11:14,936 --> 00:11:17,522
Maybe I can grill something
that's not overly fancy.

203
00:11:18,606 --> 00:11:20,525
-A chance to earn girlfriend points.
-[groans]

204
00:11:23,236 --> 00:11:24,070
[grunts]

205
00:11:26,239 --> 00:11:27,365
[grunting continues]

206
00:11:28,616 --> 00:11:29,450
[yelps]

207
00:11:31,119 --> 00:11:34,705
This whole night!
You set all this up, didn't you?

208
00:11:34,789 --> 00:11:36,040
Well, duh.

209
00:11:36,124 --> 00:11:37,041
[groans]

210
00:11:37,125 --> 00:11:39,293
You even planted that bug!

211
00:11:39,377 --> 00:11:42,463
Sure, but thanks to me,
your evening is about to heat up.

212
00:11:42,547 --> 00:11:44,048
Ugh, this is all your fault.

213
00:11:44,132 --> 00:11:46,801
Not gonna lie, I was hoping
it would turn out like this.

214
00:11:48,052 --> 00:11:50,346
-I'm so scared.
-I've got you.

215
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:53,558
[Riri] I got to say,
I didn't think you'd tackle him.

216
00:11:54,142 --> 00:11:57,812
[chuckles]
And that scream, like a bad word game.

217
00:11:57,895 --> 00:12:01,566
Shut up! I'll have you know
my scream is perfectly normal.

218
00:12:01,649 --> 00:12:02,817
[Riri] I was pretty impressed

219
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:05,027
that you were able to get him
on the floor so easily.

220
00:12:05,111 --> 00:12:07,572
That was a steamy moment
in the making, but no.

221
00:12:07,655 --> 00:12:10,324
Are you seriously judging me?

222
00:12:10,408 --> 00:12:11,576
Look!

223
00:12:11,659 --> 00:12:14,579
-You're the one causing all this trouble.
-[thunder clapping]

224
00:12:14,662 --> 00:12:18,374
Don't fret.
I got everything under control.

225
00:12:18,458 --> 00:12:20,418
[Anzu] You call that "under control"?

226
00:12:20,501 --> 00:12:22,170
[Riri] I can fix that. No problem.

227
00:12:22,670 --> 00:12:26,507
Chill up. It's time to blow him away
with your cooking skills.

228
00:12:26,591 --> 00:12:30,219
Remember, the way to a man's heart
is through his stomach.

229
00:12:30,303 --> 00:12:33,222
[Anzu] I only know how to cook stir-fry.

230
00:12:33,306 --> 00:12:36,392
Stir-fry? That's perfect!
[laughs]

231
00:12:36,476 --> 00:12:38,644
You can make Caprese sautée chicken?

232
00:12:38,728 --> 00:12:42,231
Or blue crab with eggs and sauce?

233
00:12:42,315 --> 00:12:43,232
Get real!

234
00:12:44,066 --> 00:12:45,109
[gasps]

235
00:12:45,193 --> 00:12:48,321
Why would I bother making
a good impression on this guy, anyway?

236
00:12:48,821 --> 00:12:50,781
MISO, SOY SAUCE

237
00:12:50,865 --> 00:12:52,825
Do you want miso or soy sauce?

238
00:12:54,327 --> 00:12:55,286
Miso.

239
00:12:55,369 --> 00:12:58,623
I handed you romance on a silver platter!

240
00:12:58,706 --> 00:13:00,249
[Riri screams]

241
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,210
[Tsukasa] Thanks for dinner.

242
00:13:04,295 --> 00:13:05,379
Oh, man.

243
00:13:07,590 --> 00:13:08,799
Hmm…

244
00:13:08,883 --> 00:13:13,262
I'm here to grant girls like you
who reject all opportunities of romance

245
00:13:13,346 --> 00:13:17,308
a chance to experience love
through this dating game.

246
00:13:18,142 --> 00:13:19,894
[Anzu] If that thing is causing all this,

247
00:13:19,977 --> 00:13:22,813
it's a safe bet
the storm won't let up till morning.

248
00:13:23,439 --> 00:13:26,192
You picked the wrong girl to mess with.

249
00:13:28,694 --> 00:13:30,905
You wanna play? Let's play.

250
00:13:31,906 --> 00:13:32,740
[pants]

251
00:13:33,241 --> 00:13:34,408
-[Anzu] Kazuki!
-Huh?

252
00:13:34,909 --> 00:13:37,036
-[thunderclaps]
-Spend the night.

253
00:13:37,662 --> 00:13:39,789
Yeah, I think I'll pass on that.

254
00:13:41,874 --> 00:13:44,794
Do not fear.
There'll be no funny business.

255
00:13:45,670 --> 00:13:47,547
[Tsukasa] That's, uh, reassuring.

256
00:13:47,630 --> 00:13:51,342
Great! It's settled then.
Bath time! I'll fill up the tub.

257
00:13:51,425 --> 00:13:52,552
Huh?

258
00:13:52,635 --> 00:13:54,220
Uh…

259
00:13:55,137 --> 00:13:57,640
[light music]

260
00:14:01,769 --> 00:14:04,146
[Anzu] Here, these are my dad's,
but they should fit you.

261
00:14:04,230 --> 00:14:05,064
[Tsukasa] Thanks.

262
00:14:06,691 --> 00:14:08,192
You don't want to go first?

263
00:14:08,276 --> 00:14:10,736
Of course not. Guests always go first.

264
00:14:11,445 --> 00:14:12,280
Hm.

265
00:14:14,198 --> 00:14:17,535
[giggles]
I knew you couldn't resist forever.

266
00:14:17,618 --> 00:14:21,330
Now, you're spending the night together.
Next stop, romance!

267
00:14:21,414 --> 00:14:23,499
[evil laughter]

268
00:14:26,377 --> 00:14:27,378
Hmm.

269
00:14:28,796 --> 00:14:30,506
So, I'll take the couch.

270
00:14:32,383 --> 00:14:34,218
This blanket should be warm enough.

271
00:14:35,177 --> 00:14:36,053
Huh?

272
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,393
Thanks for the bath, Hoshino.

273
00:14:42,476 --> 00:14:46,022
[Anzu] No worries.
Oh, you didn't change your shirt?

274
00:14:46,606 --> 00:14:48,399
-Yeah, not really my style.
-[meows]

275
00:14:49,525 --> 00:14:51,527
It was the only one I could find for you.

276
00:14:51,611 --> 00:14:53,613
It would have been
kind of funny to see it on.

277
00:14:56,616 --> 00:14:58,618
[Anzu exhales]
That's much better!

278
00:15:03,664 --> 00:15:05,041
Ah…

279
00:15:05,124 --> 00:15:06,542
-So lame!
-So lame!

280
00:15:06,626 --> 00:15:08,336
What's with the tucked-in shirt?

281
00:15:08,419 --> 00:15:10,463
You are not making this easy on me.

282
00:15:10,546 --> 00:15:12,548
You're the one who told me to bundle up.

283
00:15:13,758 --> 00:15:17,553
Consider it boy repellent. No chance
for romance when I'm dressed like this.

284
00:15:17,637 --> 00:15:19,680
Oh, no. Is she kidding…

285
00:15:19,764 --> 00:15:23,059
Abandoning all of her self-respect
to resist romance.

286
00:15:23,935 --> 00:15:26,771
So, Kazuki, wanna play a little game?

287
00:15:27,396 --> 00:15:28,314
[Tsukasa] What game?

288
00:15:29,190 --> 00:15:31,817
[Anzu] How about these?
I can't play them alone, you know.

289
00:15:32,568 --> 00:15:35,071
Okay. But I'm pretty good at these.

290
00:15:35,154 --> 00:15:38,282
Great! A worthy challenger.
This should be really fun.

291
00:15:41,911 --> 00:15:43,204
What?

292
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:47,208
[groaning]

293
00:15:49,794 --> 00:15:51,295
Uh, ugh…

294
00:15:53,506 --> 00:15:54,882
Ooh…

295
00:15:57,426 --> 00:16:01,097
-All right!
-Why can't I beat you?

296
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:02,306
[laughs]

297
00:16:02,390 --> 00:16:05,726
You're gonna have to put in a lot
more work if you wanna beat me at games.

298
00:16:06,310 --> 00:16:08,729
[Tsukasa] You don't have
to be a brat about it.

299
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:10,523
-Ugh…
-Huh?

300
00:16:11,273 --> 00:16:12,733
I challenge you to a game of luck.

301
00:16:13,317 --> 00:16:15,319
Let's see how you do
without your strategies.

302
00:16:16,612 --> 00:16:20,032
Ha! Fine, but whoever loses
has to make lunch,

303
00:16:20,116 --> 00:16:22,243
and I'll take two desserts, thanks.

304
00:16:22,827 --> 00:16:25,162
-Slow down there.
-[Anzu] Game on, you're going down.

305
00:16:25,246 --> 00:16:26,998
I am gonna be a billionaire.

306
00:16:27,081 --> 00:16:28,249
[laughs]

307
00:16:28,958 --> 00:16:31,585
[Riri] On that stormy night
at the Hoshino house,

308
00:16:31,669 --> 00:16:34,255
an epic board game battle began.

309
00:16:34,922 --> 00:16:39,343
Anzu, in her frumpiest PJ's,
completely ignoring a chance of romance.

310
00:16:39,427 --> 00:16:43,014
Kazuki with his best poker face,
seeking revenge.

311
00:16:43,097 --> 00:16:45,266
Each player oblivious to the situation.

312
00:16:45,349 --> 00:16:48,310
Each determined to be the winner!

313
00:16:50,396 --> 00:16:51,355
[Anzu] Hm.

314
00:16:51,439 --> 00:16:53,774
[rattling, chiming]

315
00:16:53,858 --> 00:16:56,652
[Anzu] Hm, hm, hm, hm, hm…

316
00:16:56,736 --> 00:16:57,778
Hm?

317
00:16:57,862 --> 00:17:01,282
"You damaged a luxury car.
Pay 10,000 dollars."?

318
00:17:01,365 --> 00:17:02,950
I'm in debt already!

319
00:17:03,034 --> 00:17:04,285
-[wails]
-[scoffs]

320
00:17:04,368 --> 00:17:05,286
[game spinner rattling]

321
00:17:06,328 --> 00:17:07,788
[Tsukasa] Hm, hm…

322
00:17:07,872 --> 00:17:11,834
"You found an antique vase.
Collect the five-thousand-dollar reward."

323
00:17:11,917 --> 00:17:13,836
[Anzu] Who loses something like that?

324
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:15,421
Grrr.

325
00:17:16,505 --> 00:17:17,840
-[grunts]
-[game spinner rattling]

326
00:17:17,923 --> 00:17:19,884
"The gambling habit caught up to you.

327
00:17:19,967 --> 00:17:23,345
You lose all your money
at the races." Seriously?

328
00:17:24,096 --> 00:17:26,057
[groans, sighs]

329
00:17:29,143 --> 00:17:30,936
[Tsukasa] Hm, hm, hm…

330
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:35,566
"You sold your macho men figures
to a collector. Earn 50,000 dollars."

331
00:17:36,150 --> 00:17:39,487
Come on! It's not fair!
You're landing on all the good stuff.

332
00:17:39,570 --> 00:17:42,573
Hey, don't blame me.
Luck's on my side tonight.

333
00:17:42,656 --> 00:17:43,824
[gasps]

334
00:17:44,784 --> 00:17:46,077
[evil laughter]

335
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:48,621
[Anzu] So, that's how you wanna play?

336
00:17:49,663 --> 00:17:54,251
Grr. I will not lose!

337
00:17:55,169 --> 00:17:57,421
"You step in dog poop
and ruined your Jimmy Choo's.

338
00:17:57,505 --> 00:17:59,340
Replace them for 10,000 dollars."

339
00:17:59,423 --> 00:18:02,843
Who wears expensive shoes
like that to walk their dogs?

340
00:18:03,928 --> 00:18:06,847
"The shock of stepping in dog poop
makes you drop 10,000 dollars."

341
00:18:06,931 --> 00:18:08,849
[screams]
No!

342
00:18:10,518 --> 00:18:11,352
Hm?

343
00:18:11,435 --> 00:18:14,814
"You dog, Pochi,
dug up Tokugawa's buried treasure.

344
00:18:14,897 --> 00:18:16,482
Collect one million dollars."

345
00:18:16,565 --> 00:18:19,610
-[Anzu] What?
-[Tsukasa] Good boy, Pochi.

346
00:18:20,861 --> 00:18:23,197
[Anzu grunts]
…two, three, four.

347
00:18:23,280 --> 00:18:26,283
"You step in dog poop
and ruined your Jimmy Choo's.

348
00:18:26,367 --> 00:18:29,620
Replace them for 10,000 dollars."
Not again!

349
00:18:30,204 --> 00:18:32,123
[Tsukasa] How many times
you're gonna step in poop?

350
00:18:32,206 --> 00:18:34,625
-Yeah? Laugh it up! Go on!
-[Tsukasa giggles]

351
00:18:34,708 --> 00:18:38,629
[Anzu] Your dog's probably the one leaving
all that poop on my side of the street!

352
00:18:39,421 --> 00:18:41,382
Don't accuse my Pochi like that.

353
00:18:43,384 --> 00:18:45,094
[miniature plane tapping]

354
00:18:45,177 --> 00:18:47,096
Huh? Guess I won.

355
00:18:48,222 --> 00:18:49,849
What?

356
00:18:49,932 --> 00:18:53,102
Didn't have to put in that much more work
in order to beat you after all.

357
00:18:53,727 --> 00:18:55,104
[grunts angrily]

358
00:18:55,187 --> 00:18:57,273
Looks like Anzu lost. Too bad!

359
00:18:57,356 --> 00:18:59,650
-I'll show you!
-[grunts]

360
00:19:01,735 --> 00:19:03,654
[Anzu] This is such a drag.

361
00:19:03,737 --> 00:19:06,407
Why did I have to go
and open my big mouth?

362
00:19:07,032 --> 00:19:07,867
Huh?

363
00:19:08,659 --> 00:19:10,077
I thought I should help…

364
00:19:10,619 --> 00:19:13,038
since I lost the first game.

365
00:19:13,122 --> 00:19:15,374
[gasps]
Thank you!

366
00:19:15,457 --> 00:19:18,043
Feel free to use whatever
is in the fridge.

367
00:19:18,127 --> 00:19:19,420
You're the best!

368
00:19:20,754 --> 00:19:23,174
Come on, you have to
at least make something.

369
00:19:23,257 --> 00:19:24,967
-I mean you are the loser.
-[sighs]

370
00:19:25,634 --> 00:19:26,760
Don't rub it in.

371
00:19:34,268 --> 00:19:36,187
[Tsukasa] Do you always
put sugar in your eggs?

372
00:19:36,770 --> 00:19:39,273
Of course. That's how you make it.

373
00:19:40,524 --> 00:19:42,776
-Probably pineapple in your pork?
-Duh.

374
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:45,029
-Potato apple salad?
-Delicious!

375
00:19:45,112 --> 00:19:46,447
[sighs]

376
00:19:46,530 --> 00:19:48,199
You really are a weirdo.

377
00:19:48,782 --> 00:19:50,910
[Anzu] Weird or not,
I'm the one making the eggs,

378
00:19:50,993 --> 00:19:54,705
so I'll prepare them
how I like them, plain and simple.

379
00:19:55,831 --> 00:19:57,791
[sizzling]

380
00:19:58,792 --> 00:20:00,628
[humming]

381
00:20:02,796 --> 00:20:04,715
[humming angrily]

382
00:20:04,798 --> 00:20:06,175
[growling]

383
00:20:07,176 --> 00:20:10,721
Huh? Is that supposed
to be scrambled eggs?

384
00:20:10,804 --> 00:20:13,766
[Anzu] For your information,
they don't always turn out this bad.

385
00:20:13,849 --> 00:20:15,768
Maybe you just need
a little more practice.

386
00:20:15,851 --> 00:20:16,727
[Anzu sighs]

387
00:20:19,688 --> 00:20:21,732
[Anzu] Kazuki, these look delicious!

388
00:20:22,274 --> 00:20:23,817
Ah, mm.

389
00:20:23,901 --> 00:20:25,736
Mmm… Mm!

390
00:20:25,819 --> 00:20:29,156
These are crazy good!
Who knew you are such a pro.

391
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:32,284
Well, I've been working part-time
in the kitchen of a local bar.

392
00:20:32,910 --> 00:20:35,621
Slow down.
Save some for lunch for tomorrow.

393
00:20:36,330 --> 00:20:37,581
[in muffled voice]
What? I'm hungry.

394
00:20:37,665 --> 00:20:39,750
A girl can't live
on instant noodles alone.

395
00:20:39,833 --> 00:20:41,752
-I guess I should have made more.
-Hm…

396
00:20:41,835 --> 00:20:46,048
Or you can make some extra now,
so I can have some more tomorrow.

397
00:20:46,131 --> 00:20:47,258
Hm.

398
00:20:47,341 --> 00:20:49,510
-[Anzu] Don't be shy. Use the whole bag!
-Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

399
00:20:49,593 --> 00:20:51,262
[Tsukasa] Stop! That's too much.

400
00:20:51,345 --> 00:20:54,932
[Anzu] Looks so good!
[yelps, chuckles]

401
00:20:55,015 --> 00:20:57,935
Oh, man! You even made octopus!

402
00:20:58,477 --> 00:21:00,479
You can't have homemade lunch
without octopus.

403
00:21:00,562 --> 00:21:01,397
[Anzu] Hmm…

404
00:21:07,069 --> 00:21:08,779
[Anzu] He's not at all
what I thought he was

405
00:21:08,862 --> 00:21:10,572
from my first impression.

406
00:21:10,656 --> 00:21:12,658
[bright music]

407
00:21:20,416 --> 00:21:22,835
Everyone thinks he's this standoffish guy

408
00:21:22,918 --> 00:21:25,421
but he's actually pretty easy to talk to.

409
00:21:25,504 --> 00:21:27,464
I feel like I could tell him anything.

410
00:21:28,299 --> 00:21:29,133
[gasps]

411
00:21:29,216 --> 00:21:32,428
I am not developing feelings for him.
Not that he's interested.

412
00:21:32,511 --> 00:21:35,347
Besides, I haven't earned
any girlfriend points.

413
00:21:36,307 --> 00:21:38,851
[Anzu] How about I beat you
at a game of cards next?

414
00:21:38,934 --> 00:21:42,813
-Okay, just gotta use the restroom first.
-Sounds good.

415
00:21:44,440 --> 00:21:47,359
[Anzu] When did it get so late?
I'm not even tired.

416
00:21:48,152 --> 00:21:50,404
We can play Speed or Concentration.

417
00:21:50,487 --> 00:21:52,323
[squeals]
So many options.

418
00:21:52,406 --> 00:21:54,992
-[Riri] What are you doing?
-Ugh, you again?

419
00:21:55,075 --> 00:21:58,746
Why are you wasting time
playing games like a bunch of little kids?

420
00:21:58,829 --> 00:22:03,167
Watch a rom-com, flirt.
Give in to the romance of it all.

421
00:22:03,250 --> 00:22:05,461
-No one asked you!
-Oh, sad.

422
00:22:05,544 --> 00:22:07,046
You couldn't even achieve the classic

423
00:22:07,129 --> 00:22:08,964
-run-into-each-other-in-the-bath scene.
-Grr.

424
00:22:09,548 --> 00:22:12,092
Try it and you and that wand
will get better acquainted.

425
00:22:12,760 --> 00:22:16,430
So, maybe I should have cast
that spell on you after all.

426
00:22:16,513 --> 00:22:18,223
[scoffs]
Sorry to disappoint,

427
00:22:18,307 --> 00:22:20,434
but there is no chance this goes your way.

428
00:22:20,517 --> 00:22:23,145
-Really?
-[yells]

429
00:22:24,354 --> 00:22:25,189
Ow!

430
00:22:30,444 --> 00:22:33,238
It's time for all good children
to go to sleep.

431
00:22:36,742 --> 00:22:38,410
-What?
-[snores]

432
00:22:38,494 --> 00:22:41,163
Looks like she passed out. That was fast!

433
00:22:42,915 --> 00:22:46,794
Hoshino, if you're gonna sleep,
go to your room. Wake up!

434
00:22:47,878 --> 00:22:48,796
Hm.

435
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:57,888
Now, what'd I do?

436
00:22:58,388 --> 00:22:59,223
Hm?

437
00:22:59,848 --> 00:23:01,558
Shouldn't sleep with your glasses on.

438
00:23:02,684 --> 00:23:03,769
[moans]

439
00:23:03,852 --> 00:23:04,853
[grunts]

440
00:23:05,687 --> 00:23:07,106
[moans]

441
00:23:09,149 --> 00:23:10,442
Mmm…

442
00:23:10,526 --> 00:23:13,320
Momohiki, I'll never let go, ever!

443
00:23:13,403 --> 00:23:15,781
Momohiki? Who the heck is that?

444
00:23:17,282 --> 00:23:18,909
-[Anzu grunts]
-[Tsukasa] What a grip!

445
00:23:20,285 --> 00:23:22,412
[sighs]
Jeez.

446
00:23:24,581 --> 00:23:26,750
I haven't had
that much fun in a long time.

447
00:23:27,459 --> 00:23:30,003
[cheerful music]

448
00:23:36,093 --> 00:23:38,637
-[chuckles]
-[snores]

449
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:39,721
What a weirdo.

450
00:23:44,977 --> 00:23:46,520
A fanfare, please!

451
00:23:46,603 --> 00:23:48,647
And a big congratulations!

452
00:23:48,730 --> 00:23:50,774
Did you fall for my little trick?

453
00:23:50,858 --> 00:23:54,194
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

454
00:23:54,278 --> 00:23:57,823
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

455
00:23:57,906 --> 00:24:00,576
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

456
00:24:00,659 --> 00:24:02,953
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

457
00:24:03,036 --> 00:24:05,622
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

458
00:24:05,706 --> 00:24:07,624
So I can make sure I get paid.

459
00:24:07,708 --> 00:24:09,877
[closing theme music]

460
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:10,794
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

461
00:24:13,422 --> 00:24:14,256
♪ Let's go! ♪

462
00:24:16,675 --> 00:24:17,926
♪ Lo-love! ♪

463
00:24:20,012 --> 00:24:20,846
♪ Here we go! ♪

464
00:00:01,828 --> 00:00:05,373
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

465
00:00:05,456 --> 00:00:08,126
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

466
00:00:08,209 --> 00:00:10,503
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

467
00:00:10,586 --> 00:00:13,172
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

468
00:00:13,256 --> 00:00:15,174
So I can make sure I get paid.

469
00:00:15,258 --> 00:00:17,427
[closing theme music]

470
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:18,344
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

471
00:00:20,972 --> 00:00:21,806
♪ Let's go! ♪

472
00:00:24,225 --> 00:00:25,476
♪ Lo-love! ♪

473
00:00:27,562 --> 00:00:28,396
♪ Here we go! ♪

